# Git workflow

- Default branch is `master`. Never commit to it, never push to it, never force-push.
- All changes land through a pull request. Merge on GitHub is the only way `master` moves.
- Sign every commit with GPG key `D5989ED9D348AA77` (`Emad Helmi <s.emad.helmi@gmail.com>`). Do not change global git config. Use:

```bash
git -c user.name="Emad Helmi" \
    -c user.email="s.emad.helmi@gmail.com" \
    -c user.signingkey=D5989ED9D348AA77 \
    -c commit.gpgsign=true \
    commit -S -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
type: short why.

EOF
)"
```

- Branch names: `<type>/<NNN>-<kebab-description>`
  - Types: `feat`, `fix`, `bugfix`, `imp`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `perf`, `hotfix`
  - `NNN` is a 3-digit increment (`001`, `002`, …). Look at existing local/remote branches before picking the next number.
  - Description is lowercase kebab-case, no spaces.
  - Valid: `feat/001-repo-foundation`, `bugfix/014-preview-lists`, `imp/003-agent-tables`
  - Invalid: `feature/foo`, `feat/1-foo`, `Feat/001-Foo`, `feat/001_foo`
- Conventional commits: `feat`, `fix`, `docs`, `chore`, `refactor`, `test`, `ci`, `perf`. Reference GitHub issues as `#<n>` when relevant.
- Prefer squash or rebase into `master` so history stays linear.
